{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-12T19:57:45.186Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-1","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ef0a31908b232616bff09378","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-1","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.269","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-wzmbvn"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Published-package verification gives up before npm metadata propagates: two consecutive scheduled cuts were recorded as failed and re-run by hand while the artifact was already live"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"## Observed\nOn 2026-09-11 (Release run 34576128355) and 2026-09-12 (Release run 34681372798) the tag-push Release workflow published the package successfully, then failed its own \"Verify published package on npm, npx, and bunx\" step on the first attempt. scripts/release/verify-published-release.mjs polls npm view for the exact version with a default of 20 attempts 15 seconds apart (about 5 minutes) and gave up with npm error code E404 \"No match found for version\". The npm registry's own time stamp for the version shows the metadata became visible 8 min 14 s (2026.9.11) and 6 min 10 s (2026.9.12) after the publish step finished. Both days the maintainer re-ran the failed job by hand about ten minutes later; attempt 2 passed on its first poll and the blocker issue (#1235, #1239) was closed.\n\n## Why it matters\nThe scheduled auto-release run watches the Release workflow and records release-workflow as its failing stage, so two correct, on-time publications count as scheduled failures in the rolling rate pm-e70zh5 measures, a blocker issue is opened for each, and a human must intervene to finish a release that already succeeded. The verifier's ceiling is a constant fitted to an earlier registry latency; nothing compares it with the lag the registry actually exhibits.\n\n## Non-goals\nNot a retry of npm publish (publication was correct both days). Not the direct-main analyzer refusal (pm-2ksptv). Not the same-day second-release policy (pm-uenmu9)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:scripts","auto-release","ci","npm","release","reliability"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-12T19:57:45.186Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-12T19:57:45.186Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The default npm metadata wait in verify-published-release.mjs is at least fifteen minutes, above the six-to-eight-minute lag measured on 2026-09-11 and 2026-09-12, and the usage text states the default; The release.yml verify step and job timeouts accommodate the longer wait and the ci-workflow contract spec pins the new job budget with the auto-release budget still at least thirty minutes larger; A unit spec proves the default attempt count without passing --npm-attempts; The next scheduled cut after the change passes attempt 1 or fails for a cause other than npm metadata propagation, recorded on pm-e70zh5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-u9d0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A scheduled cut whose publish-to-visible lag stays under the verifier's wait budget passes the Release workflow on attempt 1 with no manual re-run and no blocker issue."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"2026-09-11 and 2026-09-12 attempt 1 failed E404 after 20x15s while npm made the version visible 8m14s and 6m10s after publish; attempt 2 by hand passed on its first poll."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-e70zh5","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-09-12T19:57:45.186Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-zzylb9","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-09-12T19:57:45.186Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"a9bbbb521d901dca3df71d9c9bcc06fd32bb45262e5be3626dffbee179dccca6","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"32ee28f81b7e8a1986bcb4cbbf1ad81231501995dbc9b2ac803243b20acf4b38"}
